{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1556937103,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4OTI4NjY1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3385#issuecomment-489286658"},"message":"Sounds like a useful idea, though I'm unsure whether something like that should be part of `run` itself.  I played around a bit with creating a wrapper script (included at end of post) that would tee stdout and stderr to separate files.  With that, you could do `datalad run ./utee ...` and get the stdout and stderr in `.utee/std{out,err}-ID`.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDemo wrapper\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Tee stdout and stderr to unique (and separate) output files.\n\nThese output files will be placed under the directory .utee/ within\nthe current directory.\n\nUsage:  utee CMD [ARG ...]\n        utee '\u003cshell command\u003e'  # =\u003e sh -c '\u003cshell command\u003e'\n\"\"\"\nimport asyncio\nimport os\nimport time\nimport uuid\n\n# The asyncio subprocess code is modified from\n# https://kevinmccarthy.org/2016/07/25/streaming-subprocess-stdin-and-stdout-with-asyncio-in-python/\n\n\nasync def read_stream(stream, cb):\n    while True:\n        line = await stream.readline()\n        if line:\n            cb(line)\n        else:\n            break\n\n\nasync def stream_subprocess(program, args, stdout_cb, stderr_cb):\n    process = await asyncio.create_subprocess_exec(\n        program,\n        *args,\n        stdout=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE,\n        stderr=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE)\n    await asyncio.wait([read_stream(process.stdout, stdout_cb),\n                        read_stream(process.stderr, stderr_cb)])\n    return await process.wait()\n\n\ndef execute(program, args, stdout_cb, stderr_cb):\n    loop = asyncio.get_event_loop()\n    rc = loop.run_until_complete(\n        stream_subprocess(program, args, stdout_cb, stderr_cb))\n    loop.close()\n    return rc\n\n\ndef write(streams, msg, encoding=\"utf-8\"):\n    for stream in streams:\n        stream.write(msg.decode(encoding=encoding))\n\n\ndef generate_output_files():\n    pid = \"{}-{}\".format(time.strftime(\"%Y%m%d-%H%M%S\"),\n                         str(uuid.uuid4())[:4])\n    return [os.path.join(\".utee\", \"{}-{}\".format(stream, pid))\n            for stream in [\"stdout\", \"stderr\"]]\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    from functools import partial\n    import locale\n    import sys\n\n    if sys.version_info \u003c (3, 5):\n        sys.stderr.write(\"Python 3.5 or above required\\n\")\n        exit(1)\n\n    if len(sys.argv) == 1 or sys.argv[1] in [\"-h\", \"--help\"]:\n        sys.stderr.write(__doc__)\n        exit(1)\n    prog, *args = sys.argv[1:]\n    if not args:\n        args = [\"-c\", prog]\n        prog = \"/bin/sh\"\n\n    os.makedirs(\".utee\", exist_ok=True)\n    f_stdout, f_stderr = generate_output_files()\n\n    encoding = locale.getpreferredencoding(False)\n    try:\n        with open(f_stdout, \"w\") as stdout_fh:\n            with open(f_stderr, \"w\") as stderr_fh:\n                rc = execute(\n                    prog, args,\n                    partial(write, [sys.stdout, stdout_fh],\n                            encoding=encoding),\n                    partial(write, [sys.stderr, stderr_fh],\n                            encoding=encoding))\n    except Exception as exc:\n        sys.stderr.write(\"execution failed: {}\\n\".format(str(exc)))\n        exit(126)\n    exit(rc)\n```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1556937114,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIzMTg3OTE0MzQ="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1557149000,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4OTYxODUyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3385#issuecomment-489618522"},"message":"I think it might indeed be nice to provide such optional (e.g. bool config option like `datalad.run.sidecars`) feature to automagically create and store std output files.  Flexibility via wrappers would still be allowed by disabling it, but it would make it eas(ier) for an average Joe to benefit from it.","files":null}]}